  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our joggers manufacturing follows a structured process designed to ensure consistent fit, fabric quality, and construction durability. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Joggers require particular attention to fabric pre-shrinking and dimensional stability to ensure consistent fit after laundering.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with specification review, where we analyze your requirements including fabric preferences (fleece or terry), fit type (slim or relaxed), size chart, pocket configuration, and waistband details. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining design intent. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins. For joggers, we pay particular attention to waistband elasticity and cuff construction specifications.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and pre-shrinking follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Jogger fabrics undergo pre-shrinking treatment before cutting to minimize dimensional changes after washing. We test fabrics for shrinkage in both warp and weft directions, ensuring that finished garments maintain their measurements after laundering. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors or weights, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage for testing.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for joggers takes 15-20 days. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining fit details, pocket placement, and cuff proportions. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications and conduct wash testing to verify dimensional stability. Jogger samples require particular attention to waistband fit and cuff construction to ensure they maintain their shape through wear and washing. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design.</p>
        
        <p>Dimensional stability testing is a critical step in jogger sampling that we conduct on all fabric lots. We measure garments before and after washing to verify that shrinkage remains within acceptable tolerances (typically less than 3% in either direction). This testing ensures that the fit customers experience in unwashed garments is maintained after home laundering. Dimensional stability testing reduces returns due to fit changes after washing and is particularly important for cotton-based fabrics that have higher shrinkage potential.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for joggers requires careful attention to proportional scaling, particularly for tapered styles. The relationship between waist, hip, and ankle measurements must be maintained through grading to ensure that the silhouette remains consistent across sizes. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for this relationship, producing size sets from XS to 4XL that maintain proportional fit. Grading takes 3-5 days and includes verification of taper consistency, cuff width scaling, and pocket placement proportionality.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for joggers spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt, with complex styles such as cargo joggers requiring 35-45 days. Cutting is performed with attention to pattern alignment to ensure consistent grain direction, which affects fit and appearance. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in fleece and terry construction, with particular expertise in elastic application, pocket construction, and cuff attachment. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, elastic tension, and pocket alignment. Throughout production, we conduct in-line testing of waistband elasticity and cuff construction.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for jogger-specific criteria. Inspection includes measurement verification against graded size charts, wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, and pocket functionality testing. We also conduct elastic tension testing to ensure waistbands maintain appropriate recovery after stretching. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment, and any defects found are rectified before goods leave our facility.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to jogger performance, affecting warmth, comfort, durability, and care requirements. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different climates, seasons, and performance requirements. All fabrics are pre-shrunk and tested for dimensional stability to ensure consistent fit after laundering.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton fleece is the traditional choice for joggers, providing warmth, softness, and natural comfort. Cotton fleece typically ranges from 280-320 GSM, with heavier weights providing more warmth for cold weather. The fabric features a brushed interior that traps heat against the body, making it ideal for fall and winter wear. Cotton fleece is breathable and absorbs moisture, though it retains moisture more than synthetic alternatives. We offer combed cotton fleece for enhanced softness and reduced pilling. Cotton fleece is our recommendation for classic jogger styling and customers prioritizing natural fibers.</p>
        
        <p>French terry features a looped interior texture that provides moisture-wicking properties and a distinctive hand feel. French terry is lighter than fleece, typically in the 240-280 GSM range, making it suitable for transitional seasons and active casual wear. The looped texture increases surface area for moisture evaporation, making French terry more breathable than fleece. French terry can be produced from cotton, polyester, or blends, with cotton providing natural comfort and polyester enhancing durability. French terry is ideal for spring collections and customers who prefer lighter-weight joggers.</p>
        
        <p>Polyester fleece offers durability, color retention, and moisture-wicking properties at competitive prices. Polyester fleece typically ranges from 260-300 GSM and maintains its appearance through repeated washing without significant fading or pilling. The synthetic fiber resists shrinkage, reducing dimensional stability concerns. Polyester fleece is lighter weight than cotton fleece for equivalent warmth, making it suitable for active wear. However, polyester does not provide the natural hand feel of cotton and may retain odors more than natural fibers. Polyester fleece is ideal for value positioning and performance-focused joggers.</p>
        
        <p>Bamboo blends combine bamboo viscose with cotton or polyester for sustainable softness with performance characteristics. Bamboo fibers are naturally antimicrobial and moisture-wicking, providing odor resistance and comfort. Bamboo blends typically range from 240-280 GSM and offer a luxurious hand feel that differentiates them from conventional fleece options. The fabric has natural temperature-regulating properties, making it comfortable across a range of conditions. Bamboo blends cost approximately 15-20% more than conventional cotton but appeal to eco-conscious customers and premium positioning.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton-polyester blends combine the natural comfort of cotton with the durability and color retention of polyester. Typical blends range from 80/20 to 50/50 cotton-polyester ratios, with higher cotton content providing more natural feel and higher polyester content enhancing durability. These blends typically range from 260-300 GSM and offer balanced performance at competitive prices. The polyester component reduces shrinkage compared to 100% cotton, improving dimensional stability. Cotton-polyester blends are ideal for brands seeking a balance of natural comfort with practical performance.</p>
        
        <p>Organic cotton fleece, certified by GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard), provides sustainable options for customers prioritizing organic materials. Organic cotton is grown without synthetic pesticides or fertilizers and processed without harmful chemicals. The fabric maintains the same warmth and comfort as conventional cotton fleece with the added benefit of environmental certification. Organic cotton typically costs 15-20% more than conventional cotton but enables sustainability claims that appeal to eco-conscious consumers. GOTS certification requires traceability throughout the supply chain.</p>
        
        <p>Recycled polyester fleece, certified by GRS, provides sustainable synthetic options made from post-consumer plastic bottles. Recycled polyester offers the same durability and performance as virgin polyester with reduced environmental impact. The fabric is ideal for brands seeking sustainable options in synthetic materials. GRS certification verifies recycled content and ensures environmental and social standards in production. Recycled polyester fleece is priced similarly to virgin polyester, making sustainability accessible without significant cost premium.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Cotton Fleece</td>
              <td>280-320</td>
              <td>Warm, soft, natural, breathable</td>
              <td>Classic joggers, cold weather</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>French Terry</td>
              <td>240-280</td>
              <td>Lightweight, moisture-wicking, textured</td>
              <td>Transitional seasons, active wear</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Polyester Fleece</td>
              <td>260-300</td>
              <td>Durable, color-fast, lightweight warmth</td>
              <td>Value positioning, performance</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Bamboo Blend</td>
              <td>240-280</td>
              <td>Sustainable, antimicrobial, soft</td>
              <td>Premium, eco-conscious</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Cotton-Polyester Blend</td>
              <td>260-300</td>
              <td>Balanced performance, reduced shrinkage</td>
              <td>All-season, value positioning</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All fabrics pre-shrunk and tested for dimensional stability. Custom GSM available.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Joggers from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for joggers and casual knit garments, combining cost advantages with specialized expertise in fleece and terry production. The country's garment industry includes numerous factories focused on casual wear, with developed supply chains for cotton fleece and French terry fabrics. This specialization, combined with competitive labor costs, makes Bangladesh an attractive option for jogger manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished joggers. However, the cost advantage does not come at the expense of quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has developed particular expertise in fleece garment production, with operators skilled in handling bulky fabrics, attaching cuffs and waistbands, and constructing pockets that maintain their shape. Our facility conducts regular training programs to ensure operators are proficient in the latest jogger construction techniques.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's domestic fabric supply includes numerous mills capable of producing cotton fleece, French terry, and polyester blends suitable for jogger construction. The country has invested heavily in knitting capacity, reducing reliance on imported fabrics for basic jogger styles. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local fabric mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality for jogger fabrics. For specialized fabrics or custom weights, we maintain relationships with international fabric suppliers.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export infrastructure includes experienced freight forwarders, customs brokers, and documentation specialists familiar with garment export requirements. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Ocean freight is particularly cost-effective for bulky joggers compared to air freight, given the fabric weight. The established export infrastructure reduces the risk of delays and documentation errors that can occur with less experienced sourcing locations.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's garment sector has made substantial progress on workplace safety and social compliance since the reforms that followed 2013. Our factory holds BSCI certification, covering fair wages, reasonable working hours, and safe working conditions, and joggers brands sourcing today are sourcing from a very different compliance landscape than the one that existed a decade ago. That matters directly to retailers and consumers who now factor ethical sourcing into buying decisions, and it lowers the reputational risk that once made some brands hesitant about Bangladesh production.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs for joggers, which are subject to standard garment duty rates in many markets. For brands targeting EU distribution, the duty savings can offset other costs and improve overall margins.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in knit garment production, which directly translates to jogger manufacturing. Handling fleece and terry fabrics, attaching elastic waistbands and cuffs, and constructing garments that maintain dimensional stability are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new jogger styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs. The industry's experience with international casual wear brands also means that quality expectations for fit and finish are well-understood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship joggers to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international jogger shipments ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost, though air freight is less common for joggers due to fabric weight. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by fabric composition and declared value. Joggers typically fall under specific HS codes for cotton or synthetic trousers. We provide accurate classification and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Post-Brexit documentation requirements are handled to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to joggers. The US has specific labeling requirements for garments including fiber content in English and country of origin. We ensure all labels meet US Federal Trade Commission requirements. US customs may also inspect for compliance with textile fiber identification rules, which we address through proper documentation.</p>
        
        <p>Australia shipments take 20-25 days by ocean freight to major ports including Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane. Air freight takes 7-10 days. Australia maintains a free trade agreement with Bangladesh that eliminates duties on many garments, though specific rules of origin must be met. We ensure our production processes meet these origin requirements to qualify for duty-free entry. Australia's strict biosecurity requirements are addressed through proper packaging and documentation to prevent clearance delays.</p>
        
        <p>European Union shipments benefit from duty-free access under the Everything But Arms arrangement for least-developed countries. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days to Southern European ports. Air freight takes 5-8 days. EU countries require specific documentation including certificates of origin, commercial invoices with detailed descriptions, and conformity declarations for certain materials. The EU also has specific requirements for textile labeling including fiber content percentages and care instructions in the language of the destination country.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. For joggers, this may include certificates for fiber content if organic or recycled materials are used. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. For joggers, we typically recommend FOB for experienced importers, as the cost savings on ocean freight for bulky garments make FOB economically advantageous. CIF and DDP options are available for brands seeking simplified logistics or those new to international sourcing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our joggers manufacturing process. Joggers require particular attention to dimensional stability and construction durability due to their casual nature and frequent washing. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, social responsibility, and environmental standards.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to our fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, and formaldehyde. This certification is particularly important for joggers that have prolonged skin contact during casual wear and lounging. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, elastics, trims, and threads. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each material lot, enabling you to substantiate claims about chemical safety in your marketing materials.</p>
        
        <p>GRS (Global Recycled Standard) certification applies to our recycled polyester fabrics, verifying the recycled content and ensuring traceability throughout the supply chain. GRS certification covers environmental and social criteria for recycled material production, including wastewater treatment, chemical restrictions, and labor practices. If you choose recycled fabrics for your joggers, GRS certification provides credible substantiation for sustainability claims and is increasingly required by major retailers for recycled content products.</p>
        
        <p>GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) certification applies to our organic cotton fabrics, verifying organic fiber content and ensuring environmentally and socially responsible production. GOTS covers the entire supply chain from harvesting to labeling, ensuring that organic claims are substantiated throughout production. If you choose organic cotton for your joggers, GOTS certification provides credibility for organic marketing claims and is required by many retailers for organic textile products.</p>
        
        <p>BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification is what backs up our labor-standards claims on fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions. Independent third-party auditors carry out the audits, covering the full scope of social compliance rather than a single checkbox item. For joggers and loungewear brands, that's the kind of documentation you can hand to retail buyers or put in front of end consumers who are increasingly asking about labor practices before they purchase.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For joggers, this means consistent fit, fabric quality, and construction across orders.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance specific to jogger production. We conduct in-line inspections during production, measuring garments at critical checkpoints to verify dimensional accuracy. Final inspection includes wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, ensuring that garments maintain their fit after home laundering. We maintain records of all testing results, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery. These internal processes ensure certifications translate to actual quality in finished joggers.</p>
      </div>
