      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order quantity for joggers?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Our minimum order quantity for custom joggers is 300 pieces per style. This minimum allows you to access factory-direct pricing while testing market response with manageable inventory. The 300-piece minimum can be distributed across sizes within a single colorway. Lower quantities are available for sampling and prototype development at higher per-piece costs for brands requiring smaller initial runs or needing to test multiple styles before committing to bulk production.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What fabric options do you offer for joggers?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We offer cotton fleece for warmth and natural feel (280-320 GSM), French terry for textured comfort (240-280 GSM), polyester fleece for durability and color retention (260-300 GSM), bamboo blends for sustainable softness (240-280 GSM), and cotton-polyester blends for balanced performance (260-300 GSM). All fabrics are pre-shrunk to minimize dimensional changes after washing. Fabric selection depends on climate, season, and intended use, with heavier weights for cold weather and lighter weights for transitional seasons.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What jogger styles can you manufacture?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We manufacture slim fit joggers with tapered legs for modern styling, relaxed fit joggers for comfort and casual wear, cargo joggers with multiple pockets for functionality, track joggers with side stripes for athletic styling, and fleece-lined joggers for cold weather. All styles feature elastic waistbands with drawstring options and cuffed ankles. Custom style development is available with technical specifications. Cargo joggers typically require a 500-piece minimum due to increased production complexity.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do you offer eco-friendly jogger options?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. We offer organic cotton fleece certified by GOTS for natural fiber sustainability, recycled polyester fleece certified by GRS for synthetic material recycling, and bamboo blends for sustainable softness. All eco-friendly options maintain the same quality standards as conventional fabrics. Organic cotton costs approximately 15-20% more than conventional cotton, while recycled polyester is priced similarly to virgin polyester. Certification documentation is provided for marketing substantiation.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does jogger production take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Standard production timeline is 30-40 days from fabric receipt for basic joggers. Custom fabric development adds 15-20 days. Sampling takes 15-20 days before bulk production approval. Complex styles such as cargo joggers or fleece-lined versions may require 35-45 days production time. We recommend planning 60-75 days total from initial inquiry to delivery for first-time orders including sampling and production, or 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you produce joggers with custom pocket configurations?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. We offer standard side pockets, back patch pockets, cargo pockets with flap closures, zippered security pockets, and hidden media pockets. Custom pocket placement and sizing are available with technical specifications. Complex pocket configurations may increase minimum order quantities to 500 pieces due to production complexity. We can provide guidance on pocket construction methods that balance functionality with manufacturing efficiency, ensuring pockets maintain their shape and function through repeated use and washing.</p>
